/**
 * §26.2 process-owned tools — bus tools for 26.2 defined with `defineTools("26.2", <agent>, defs)` from
 * ../tools.ts. Every tool string must be one spec/registry/agents.json names for 26.2; src/app/tools.test.ts refuses
 * the rest. Spread by ./index.ts.
 *
 * The `closer` (title-closing agent) runs in application scope. Every act goes through the pure rules in
 * src/domain/closing/ops-26-2.ts, which append the events the timers and 26.3 / 26.4 / 27.1 / 29.x / 30.2 consume.
 * Entity-store kinds mirror migration 0094: closings, signing_sessions, enotes, mers_transactions, recordings,
 * custody_records, eclosing_eligibility, consents, documents. Ports: the eClosing/RON platform and the MERS eRegistry
 * (ops-26-2.ts ports with fakes, under rt.services "26.2.ron" / "26.2.eregistry"), the eVault (rt.ports.evault — the
 * Location's Authoritative Copy), the eRecording vendor (rt.ports.erecording — county coverage). Guardrails encode the
 * spec's sentences: never open a session with a closed gate; never require electronic records or RON of any borrower;
 * never apply, complete or "assist" a signature or notarial act; never accept a KBA/credential override; never register
 * an eNote whose hash does not match the eVault copy; never fund-related actions before the audit trail is on file;
 * never convert a paper note to an eNote; never submit a recording with a handwritten instrument change; never disable
 * the paper fallback; never a notary outside the state of the act; never treat GA/MS (or any unlisted state) as
 * RON-eligible without counsel confirmation.
 */
